          "question": "What is described as first-line drug therapy for type 2 diabetes?",
          "answer": "The first-line drug therapy for type 2 diabetes is typically metformin, particularly when there are no other compelling health conditions present. This recommendation is grounded in its long history of use, low cost, weight neutrality, and minimal risk of causing low blood sugar when used alone. In addition to medication, structured lifestyle interventions are also advised for better management of the condition. This information comes from the \"Type 2 diabetes: first-line pharmacologic management\" document.\n\nI was not able to provide specifics on alternative therapies or the latest updates in diabetic treatment beyond metformin as a first-line option.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
